---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How Mindtivate uses affiliate links and how we choose what to recommend."
>
  <section class="section container prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p>
      In accordance with the FTC's Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements
      and Testimonials, this page explains how Mindtivate uses affiliate
      relationships.
    </p>

    <h2>What that means</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on Mindtivate — for example, links to products mentioned in
      articles — are affiliate links. If you click one and make a purchase,
      we may earn a commission. This comes at no additional cost to you; the
      price you pay is the same either way. Purchases made through these
      links help support the research and writing behind Mindtivate.
    </p>

    <h2>How we choose what to recommend</h2>
    <p>
      We start from a problem raised in a real community discussion, then
      research products that address it. We only apply for affiliate
      programs for products we would already recommend, and a product is
      not published with a live affiliate link until it has been through
      that review and the affiliate application has been approved
      (tracked internally as <code>affiliateStatus</code>).
    </p>

    <h2>Where you'll see a disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Every article that includes an affiliate link carries an in-article
      disclosure near the top of the page and again next to each
      recommendation, in addition to this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about a specific link or recommendation, <a href={withBase('/contact')}>contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  code {
    background: var(--color-cream-deep);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
